# The rows of the widest draft verification step (the anchor and the most
# drafts; the executor's `MAX_DRAFT_PROPOSALS` is this minus one), and so the
# row count every decode form serves: a verification row must compute the bits
# plain decode computes for it, so every launch the row count selects up to
# it is a GEMV row class (`alike` the one-row launch) and the first launch
# beyond it (the batched form, the GEMM) starts above it. The routed and
# progressive decode forms, the decode attention and the executor's decode
# classes all read it: this is the one eight.
const VERIFY_ROWS = 8
